course: dictionary
lesson: 8682
title: Seeker: the one who looks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A seeker is a person who looks for something. The word comes from the verb seek, which means look for. In hide-and-seek, the seeker counts first and then goes off to find the others. «Ready or not, I'm coming!» tells everyone that the seeker is on the way.
explain: The word also comes after other words to show what someone wants. A «job seeker» is looking for work, and a «thrill seeker» loves exciting, risky things. To work out which meaning fits, look at the words around it: is it a game, or is it about wanting something?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The seeker counted to ten, then began to search.» If you put "the one who looks" in place of seeker, the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A seeker is a person who looks for something or tries to get something they want.
fact: In hide-and-seek, the seeker counts first and then searches for the other players.
fact: «Seeker» comes from the verb «seek», which means look for.
fact: «Job seeker» means someone looking for work; «thrill seeker» means someone who loves exciting, risky things.
fact: «Asylum seeker» means someone who has asked for protection and is waiting for an answer.
exercise: «The seeker counted to ten, then began to search for the others.» In hide-and-seek, what is the seeker's job? | To count the points at the end | *To find the other players | To hide before the others find them | To make the rules
exercise: What does «thrill seeker» mean? | *Someone who loves exciting, risky things | Someone who is scared of games | Someone who makes the thrills in films | A person who runs very fast
exercise: Seeker comes from a verb. Which word is that verb? | seed | *seek | seem | secret
test: «The job seeker filled in a form and waited for news.» What is a job seeker? | *Someone who is looking for work | A teacher at school | A boss at a big company | Someone who gives out jobs
test: Which game has a seeker who counts first and then searches? | Snakes and ladders | Football | *Hide-and-seek | Chess
exam: «An asylum seeker has asked for protection and is waiting for an answer.» What does asylum seeker mean? | *Someone who has asked for protection and is waiting for an answer | A pupil who asks many questions | A person who sells protection | A lost child looking for home
